    "cr-div-neg-zero": {
      "status": "rejected",
      "reason": "IEEE keeps the sign of a zero, and the planner does ship it (the wire operand for -0.0 is `-0`), but a query plan is JSON-encoded on its way into a Convex function and JSON.stringify(-0) is \"0\" — the sign bit is gone before the adapter sees it, so it rejects a constant zero denominator rather than guess which infinity CEL produced",
      "message": "division by a constant zero whose sign is indeterminate: a query plan is JSON-encoded on its way into a Convex function and JSON has no -0, so the adapter cannot tell +Infinity from -Infinity"
    },
